        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ". When the discriminant is positive, the quadratic has exactly two real solutions; when the discriminant is 0, the quadratic has exactly one real solution; and when the discriminant is negative, the quadratic has no real solutions. Since this quadratic has exactly one real solution, the discriminant must equal 0. The quadratic is now in standard form,",
