  {
    "url": "https://oneprep.xyz/question/2990/?question_set=princeton-review-practice-tests-question-bank&module=math&primary_class=Algebra&skill=Functions",
    "question_set": "princeton-review-practice-tests-question-bank",
    "subject": "Math",
    "difficulty": "",
    "domain": "Algebra",
    "skill": "Functions",
    "question_type": "select",
    "question_content": [
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "At the end of each year, an item loses 6% of the value that it had at the beginning of the year. What type of function best represents this scenario?",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      }
    ],
    "explanation": [
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "The question asks for a description of a function that models a specific situation. Compare the answer choices. Two choices say the function is increasing, and two say it is decreasing. The question states that",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "an item loses 6% of the value",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ". Eliminate (C) and (D) because they describe an increasing function. The difference between (A) and (B) is whether the function is exponential or linear. Determine this by plugging in an initial value of the item. Plug in $100 to make it easy to work with percents.",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "Percent",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "means out of 100, so translate 6% as",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "image",
        "content": {
          "type": "url",
          "content": "https://cdn.princetonreview.com/EvaluativeContent/DigitalSAT/3aaba943-4a54-4457-9a1c-a5c3a5ba1108_bc3dcf00-2ce1-4234-9495-7d5db8f18193.svg",
          "style": [
            "html-max-width: none; vertical-align: -15px;"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ". The value of the item decreases the first year by",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "image",
        "content": {
          "type": "url",
          "content": "https://cdn.princetonreview.com/EvaluativeContent/DigitalSAT/3aaba943-4a54-4457-9a1c-a5c3a5ba1108_e61280c1-753b-460e-8116-fb3fa866afd0.svg",
          "style": [
            "html-max-width: none; vertical-align: -15px;"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "($100) = $6. Subtract this from the original value to get $100 – $6 = $94. Now decrease the new value by 6% to get $94 –",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "image",
        "content": {
          "type": "url",
          "content": "https://cdn.princetonreview.com/EvaluativeContent/DigitalSAT/3aaba943-4a54-4457-9a1c-a5c3a5ba1108_e99af84b-3abe-42e9-97c9-5800b6e0cae9.svg",
          "style": [
            "html-max-width: none; vertical-align: -15px;"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "($94) = $94 – $5.64 = $88.36. The value decreased by $6 the first year and by $5.64 the second year. A linear function would change by the same amount every year, so eliminate (B). The relationship between the value of the item and time is exponential. The correct answer is (A).",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      }
    ],
    "answer": {
      "identifier": "A",
      "is_correct": true,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "string",
          "content": "Decreasing exponential",
          "metadata": {
            "style": []
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "options": [
      {
        "identifier": "A",
        "is_correct": true,
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "string",
            "content": "Decreasing exponential",
            "metadata": {
              "style": []
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "identifier": "B",
        "is_correct": false,
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "string",
            "content": "Decreasing linear",
            "metadata": {
              "style": []
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "identifier": "C",
        "is_correct": false,
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "string",
            "content": "Increasing exponential",
            "metadata": {
              "style": []
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "identifier": "D",
        "is_correct": false,
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "string",
            "content": "Increasing linear",
            "metadata": {
              "style": []
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "question_id": "2990",
    "knowledge_point": "None"
