          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "c",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "total yeast colonies on the count plate. What is the equation that represents this relationship, assuming that no yeast was added or removed after counting began?",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      }
    ],
    "explanation": [
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "The question asks for the equation that represents the relationship between two variables. When given a table of values and asked for the correct equation, plug values from the table into the answer choices to see which one works. According to the table,",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "s",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "= 2 when",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "c",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "= 80. Choice (A) becomes 80 = (1 + 3)",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "2",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "sup"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", or 80 = 42, then 80 = 16. This is not true, so eliminate (A). Choice (B) becomes 80 = (1 + 5)",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "2",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "sup"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", or 80 = 6",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "2",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "sup"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", then 80 = 36; eliminate (B). Choice (C) becomes 80 = 3(1 + 5)",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "2",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "sup"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", or 80 = 3(6)",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "2",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "sup"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", then 80 = 3(36), then 80 = 108; eliminate (C). Choice (D) becomes 80 = 5(1 + 3)",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "2",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "sup"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", or 80 = 5(4)",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "2",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "sup"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", then 80 = 5(16), then 80 = 80. This is true, so keep (D). The correct answer is (D).",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      }
    ],
