      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "x",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "%(–53). The graph of this function is a line going downward from left to right, so it is decreasing. Eliminate (C) and (D) because they describe an increasing function. Also eliminate (A) because the graph is a straight line, not a curve like the graph of an exponential function would be. This leaves (B) as the correct answer.",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "p"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "Another option is to plug in increasing values for",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "x",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "and compare the corresponding values of",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "g",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
