      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "A local organization rents a classroom for 5 hours at an hourly rate. The organization also pays a one-time booking fee of $5 in addition to the hourly rate. The total cost of renting the classroom is $65. What is the rate, in dollars, for renting the classroom for 1 hour?",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "blank"
      }
    ],
    "explanation": [
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "The question asks for a value given a specific situation. Translate the information in Bite-Sized Pieces. The question states that the",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "total cost of renting the classroom is $65",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ". The question also states that the organization",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "pays a one-time booking fee of $5",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ". Subtract the booking fee from the total cost to get $65 – $5 = $60. Since the organization rented the classroom for 5 hours, divide $60 by 5 to find the rate for one hour:",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "image",
        "content": {
          "type": "url",
          "content": "https://cdn.princetonreview.com/EvaluativeContent/DigitalSAT/c1188311-e04e-4fd9-a73d-cf0035f307e0_0b1f9621-629f-43ba-8ae4-95a09236c32a.svg",
