    "explanation": [
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "The question asks for the value of a constant in a system of equations. When a system of linear equations has infinitely many solutions, the two equations form the same line. One method is to enter both equations into the built-in calculator. Click to add the slider for",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "k",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", then move the slider left and right until the two lines are the same. This happens when",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "k",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "= 3, so 3 is correct.",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "p"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "To solve for",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "k",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "algebraically, start by making the two equations look similar. First, add 12",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
