          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "-axis at –20 and 4. The question asks for the negative solution, which is –20.",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "p"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "To solve algebraically, recall that, with an absolute value, the value inside the absolute value bars can be either positive or negative, so this equation has two possible solutions. To start solving for",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "x",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", treat the absolute value symbols as a term and combine like terms to get 3|8 +",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "x",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "| = 36. Next, divide both sides of the equation by 3 to get |8 +",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "x",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
