      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ")(1 ±",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "rate",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ")",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "number of changes",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ". The question states that the",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "original amount",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "is 6,500, and all of the answers include this piece. The question also states that the number",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "will decrease by 20 percent",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ". This is the",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "rate",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", and 20% in decimal form is 0.2. Because the number of cards is decreasing, the value inside the parentheses is (1 –",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "rate",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "), which is (1 – 0.2) = 0.8. Eliminate (A) and (B) because they have the wrong value inside the parentheses. The number of cards decreases once every 6 months, and the exponents in the answer choices are in terms of",
        "metadata": {
