      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ". When the discriminant is positive, the quadratic has exactly two real solutions; when the discriminant is 0, the quadratic has exactly one real solution; and when the discriminant is negative, the quadratic has no real solutions. Thus, the discriminant of this quadratic must equal a positive number. Since the quadratic is in standard form, which is",
        "metadata": {
