    "explanation": [
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "The question asks for the value of a constant in a quadratic. One method is to enter the equation into the built-in graphing calculator, then plug in each answer choice for",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "k",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "until one of them shows a graph with two solutions. Only –1 does this, so (D) is correct.",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "To determine when a quadratic equation has two real solutions algebraically, use the discriminant. The discriminant is the part of the quadratic formula under the square root sign and is written as",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "D",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "=",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "b",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "2",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "sup"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "– 4",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "ac",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ". When the discriminant is positive, the quadratic has exactly two real solutions; when the discriminant is 0, the quadratic has exactly one real solution; and when the discriminant is negative, the quadratic has no real solutions. Thus, the discriminant of this quadratic must equal a positive number. First, put the quadratic in standard form, which is",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "ax",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "2",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "sup"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "+",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "bx",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "+",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "c",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "= 0, by subtracting",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "k",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "from both sides of the equation to get 4",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "x",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "2",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "sup"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "– 5",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "x",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "–",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "k",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "= 0. Now that the quadratic is in standard form,",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "a",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "= 4,",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "b",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "= –5, and",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "c",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "=",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "–k",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ". Plug these into the discriminant formula to get",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "D",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "= (–5)",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "2",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "sup"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "– 4(4)(–",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "k",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "), or",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "D",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "= 25 + 16",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "k",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ". Since there are two real solutions, 25 + 16",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "k",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "&gt; 0. Subtract 25 from both sides of the inequality to get 16",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "k",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "&gt; –25, then divide both sides of the inequality by 16 to get",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "k",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "&gt; –1.5625. The only answer choice greater than –1.5625 is –1.",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "Using either method, the correct answer is (D).",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      }
    ],
