        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "-axis. There are two points of intersection, at (–0.5, 0) and (2.5, 0), so there are exactly two real solutions, and the answer is (B).",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "To determine the number of solutions algebraically, use the discriminant. The discriminant is the part of the quadratic formula under the square root sign and is written as",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
