          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "ac",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ". When the discriminant is positive, the quadratic has exactly two real solutions; when the discriminant is 0, the quadratic has exactly one real solution; and when the discriminant is negative, the quadratic has no real solutions. The quadratic is given in standard form,",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "ax",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
