      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "-axis, so there are no real solutions, and (D) is correct.",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "p"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "To determine when a quadratic equation has no real solutions algebraically, use the discriminant. The discriminant is the part of the quadratic formula under the square root sign and is written as",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
