      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "b",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ") = total tiles. Next, use process of elimination to get rid of answer choices that are not consistent with the labels. Since",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "b",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "is multiplied by the size of the seating area, eliminate (A) and (B) because they refer to the lab area, not the seating area. Compare the remaining answer choices. The difference is between the average number of tiles and the total number of tiles. Since",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
