        "type": "string",
        "content": "equals the total money made from selling the two types of softball equipment, 500 and 300 must be the cost per bat and the cost per glove, respectively. To find how much less the price of a glove is than the price of a bat, subtract 300 from 500: 500 – 300 = 200. Each glove costs $200 less than each bat. The correct answer is 200.",
