    "question_type": "select",
    "question_content": [
      {
        "type": "table",
        "content": "<table border=\"1\" style=\"height: 146px; width: 29.7997%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 51.9829%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">Distance<br/> (meters)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 146.527%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">Relative sound intensity</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 51.9829%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"width: 146.527%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">80.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 51.9829%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"width: 146.527%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">20.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 51.9829%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">2</td>\n<td style=\"width: 146.527%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">5.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 21px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 51.9829%; height: 21px; text-align: center;\">3</td>\n<td style=\"width: 146.527%; height: 21px; text-align: center;\">1.25</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>",
        "metadata": {
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "A sound technician is identifying the safest location to place speakers for an event. The table shows the relationship between the distance",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "d",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", in meters, that the technician is from the source of the sound and the relative sound intensity",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "I",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "of the sound. Which of the following equations best represents the relationship between",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "d",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "and",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "I",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "if nothing other than the distance is adjusted?",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      }
    ],
    "explanation": [
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "The question asks for an equation that represents the relationship between two variables. When given a table of values and asked for the correct equation, plug values from the table into the answer choices to see which one works. According to the table, when",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "d",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "= 2,",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "I",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "= 5. Plug these values into the answer choices and eliminate any that are not true. Choice (A) becomes 5 = 0.75(1 – 80)",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "2",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "sup"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", then 5 = 0.75(–79)",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "2",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "sup"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", and finally 5 = 4,680.75. This is not true, so eliminate (A). Choice (B) becomes 5 = (1 – 80)",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "2",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "sup"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", then 5 = (–79)",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "2",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "sup"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", and finally 5 = 6,241; eliminate (B). Choice (C) becomes 5 = (1 – 0.75)",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "2",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "sup"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", then 5 = (0.25)",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "2",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "sup"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", and finally 5 = 0.0625; eliminate (C). Choice (D) becomes 5 = 80(1 – 0.75)",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "2",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "sup"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", then 5 = 80(0.25)",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "2",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "sup"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", and finally 5 = 5. This is true, so keep (D). The correct answer is (D).",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      }
    ],
