  {
    "url": "https://oneprep.xyz/question/268/?question_set=college-board-question-bank&module=math&primary_class=H&skill=H.A.",
    "question_set": "college-board-question-bank",
    "subject": "Math",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "domain": "Algebra",
    "skill": "Linear equations in one variable",
    "question_type": "select",
    "question_content": [
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "Megan’s regular wage at her job is",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "p",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "dollars per hour for the first 8 hours of work in a day plus 1.5 times her regular hourly wage for work in excess of 8 hours that day. On a given day, Megan worked for 10 hours, and her total earnings for that day were $137.50. What is Megan’s regular hourly wage?",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "p"
          ],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      }
    ],
    "explanation": [
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "Choice B is correct. Since",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "p",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "represents Megan’s regular pay per hour, 1.5",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "p",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "represents the pay per hour in excess of 8 hours. Since Megan worked for 10 hours, she must have been paid",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "p",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "dollars per hour for 8 of the hours plus 1.5",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "p",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "dollars per hour for the remaining 2 hours. Therefore, since Megan earned $137.50 for the 10 hours, the situation can be represented by the equation 137.5 = 8",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "p",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "+ 2(1.5)",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "p.",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "Distributing the 2 in the equation gives 137.5 = 8",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "p",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "+ 3",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "p",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", and combining like terms gives 137.5 = 11",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "p",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ". Dividing both sides by 11 gives",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "p",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "= 12.5. Therefore, Megan’s regular wage is $12.50.",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "Choices A and C are incorrect and may be the result of calculation errors. Choice D is incorrect and may result from finding the average hourly wage that Megan earned for the 10 hours of work.",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "p"
          ]
        }
      }
    ],
    "answer": {
      "identifier": "B",
      "is_correct": true,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "string",
          "content": "$12.50",
          "metadata": {
