          ]
        },
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "p"
          ],
          "content_type": "stimulus"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "The constant 2.74 in this function estimates which of the following?",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "p"
          ],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      }
    ],
    "explanation": [
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "Choice D is correct. Since 2.74 is a constant term, it represents an actual price of gas rather than a measure of change in gas price. To determine what gas price it represents, find",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "x",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "such that",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "F",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "(",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "x",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ") = 2.74, or 2.74 = 2.74 – 0.19(",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "x",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "– 3). Subtracting 2.74 from both sides gives 0 = –0.19(",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "x",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "– 3). Dividing both sides by –0.19 results in 0 =",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "x",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "– 3, or",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "x",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "= 3. Therefore, the average price of gas is $2.74 per gallon 3 months after September 1, 2014, which is December 1, 2014.",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "Choice A is incorrect. Since 2.74 is a constant, not a multiple of",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "x",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", it cannot represent a rate of change in price. Choice B is incorrect. The difference in the average price from September 1, 2014, to December 1, 2014, is",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "F",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "(3) –",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "F",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "(0) = 2.74 – 0.19(3 – 3) – (2.74 – 0.19(0 – 3)) = 2.74 – (2.74 + 0.57) = –0.57, which is not 2.74. Choice C is incorrect. The average price per gallon on September 1, 2014, is",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "F",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "(0) = 2.74 – 0.19(0 – 3) = 2.74 + 0.57 = 3.31, which is not 2.74.",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "p"
          ]
        }
      }
    ],
