          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "The points plotted in the coordinate plane above represent the possible numbers of wallflowers and cornflowers that someone can buy at the Garden Store in order to spend exactly $24.00 total on the two types of flowers. The price of each wallflower is the same and the price of each cornflower is the same. What is the price, in dollars, of 1 cornflower?",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "p"
          ],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "blank"
      }
    ],
    "explanation": [
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "The correct answer is 1.5. The point",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "image",
        "content": {
          "type": "base64",
          "content": "data:image/png;base64,",
          "style": [
            ""
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "corresponds to the situation where 16 cornflowers and 0 wallflowers are purchased. Since the total spent on the two types of flowers is $24.00, it follows that the price of 16 cornflowers is $24.00, and the price of one cornflower is $1.50. Note that 1.5 and 3/2 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "p"
          ]
        }
      }
    ],
    "answer": "3/2",
