  {
    "url": "https://oneprep.xyz/question/289/?question_set=college-board-question-bank&module=math&primary_class=H&skill=H.D.",
    "question_set": "college-board-question-bank",
    "subject": "Math",
    "difficulty": "Hard",
    "domain": "Algebra",
    "skill": "Systems of two linear equations in two variables",
    "question_type": "select",
    "question_content": [
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "2 x + 3 y = 7"
        },
        "metadata": {
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "10 x + 15 y = 35"
        },
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "p"
          ],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "For each real number",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "r"
        },
        "metadata": {
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", which of the following points lies on the graph of each equation in the",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "xy",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "-plane for the given system?",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "p"
          ],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      }
    ],
    "explanation": [
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "Choice B is correct. The two given equations are equivalent because the second equation can be obtained from the first equation by multiplying each side of the equation by",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "5"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ". Thus, the graphs of the equations are coincident, so if a point lies on the graph of one of the equations, it also lies on the graph of the other equation. A point",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "\\left(x , y\\right)"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "lies on the graph of an equation in the",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "xy",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "-plane if and only if this point represents a solution to the equation. It is sufficient, therefore, to find the point that represents a solution to the first given equation. Substituting the",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "x",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "- and",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "y",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "-coordinates of choice B,",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "- \\frac{3 r}{2} + \\frac{7}{2}"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "and",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "r"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", for",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "x"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "and",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "y"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", respectively, in the first equation yields",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "2 \\left(- \\frac{3 r}{2} + \\frac{7}{2}\\right) + 3 r = 7"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", which is equivalent to",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "- 3 r + 7 + 3 r = 7"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", or",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "7 = 7"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ". Therefore, the point",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "\\left(- \\frac{3 r}{2} + \\frac{7}{2} , r\\right)"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "represents a solution to the first equation and thus lies on the graph of each equation in the",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "xy",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "em"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "-plane for the given system.",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "p"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "p"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "p"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "p"
          ]
        }
      }
    ],
    "answer": {
      "identifier": "B",
      "is_correct": true,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "formula",
          "content": {
            "type": "latex",
            "content": "\\left(- \\frac{3 r}{2} + \\frac{7}{2} , r\\right)"
          },
          "metadata": {
            "style": [
              "p"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "options": [
      {
        "identifier": "A",
        "is_correct": false,
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "formula",
            "content": {
              "type": "latex",
              "content": "\\left(\\frac{r}{5} + 7 , - \\frac{r}{5} + 35\\right)"
            },
            "metadata": {
              "style": [
                "p"
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "identifier": "B",
        "is_correct": true,
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "formula",
            "content": {
              "type": "latex",
              "content": "\\left(- \\frac{3 r}{2} + \\frac{7}{2} , r\\right)"
            },
            "metadata": {
              "style": [
                "p"
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "identifier": "C",
        "is_correct": false,
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "formula",
            "content": {
              "type": "latex",
              "content": "\\left(r , \\frac{2 r}{3} + \\frac{7}{3}\\right)"
            },
            "metadata": {
              "style": [
                "p"
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "identifier": "D",
        "is_correct": false,
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "formula",
            "content": {
              "type": "latex",
              "content": "\\left(r , - \\frac{3 r}{2} + \\frac{7}{2}\\right)"
            },
            "metadata": {
              "style": [
                "p"
