        "type": "image",
        "content": {
          "type": "base64",
          "content": "data:image/png;base64,",
          "style": [
            ""
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ". Also, since the laundry service wants to buy at least twice as many containers of detergent as containers of fabric softener, the number of containers of detergent should be greater than or equal to two times the number of containers of fabric softener. This can be expressed by the inequality",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "image",
        "content": {
          "type": "base64",
          "content": "data:image/png;base64,",
          "style": [
            ""
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ".",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "p"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "Choice B is incorrect because it misrepresents the relationship between the numbers of each container that the laundry service wants to buy. Choice C is incorrect because the first inequality of the system incorrectly doubles the weight per container of detergent. The weight of each container of detergent is 7.35, not 14.7 pounds. Choice D is incorrect because it doubles the weight per container of detergent and transposes the relationship between the numbers of containers.",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "p"
          ]
        }
      }
