    "question_content": [
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "A bakery sells trays of cookies. Each tray contains at least 50 cookies but no more than 60. Which of the following could be the total number of cookies on 4 trays of cookies?",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "p"
          ],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      }
    ],
    "explanation": [
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "Choice B is correct. If each tray contains the least number of cookies possible, 50 cookies, then the least number of cookies possible on 4 trays is 50 × 4 = 200 cookies. If each tray contains the greatest number of cookies possible, 60 cookies, then the greatest number of cookies possible on 4 trays is 60 × 4 = 240 cookies. If the least number of cookies on 4 trays is 200 and the greatest number of cookies is 240, then 205 could be the total number of cookies on these 4 trays of cookies because",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "image",
        "content": {
          "type": "base64",
          "content": "data:image/png;base64,",
          "style": [
            ""
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ".",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "Choices A, C, and D are incorrect. The least number of cookies on 4 trays is 200 cookies, and the greatest number of cookies on 4 trays is 240 cookies. The choices 165, 245, and 285 are each either less than 200 or greater than 240; therefore, they cannot represent the total number of cookies on 4 trays.",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      }
    ],
    "answer": {
      "identifier": "B",
      "is_correct": true,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "string",
          "content": "205",
          "metadata": {
