    "question_content": [
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "Ken is working this summer as part of a crew on a farm. He earned $8 per hour for the first 10 hours he worked this week. Because of his performance, his crew leader raised his salary to $10 per hour for the rest of the week. Ken saves 90% of his earnings from each week. What is the least number of hours he must work the rest of the week to save at least $270 for the week?",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "p"
          ],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      }
    ],
    "explanation": [
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "Choice C is correct. Ken earned $8 per hour for the first 10 hours he worked, so he earned a total of $80 for the first 10 hours he worked. For the rest of the week, Ken was paid at the rate of $10 per hour. Let",
        "metadata": {
