    "question_content": [
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "An event planner is planning a party. It costs the event planner a onetime fee of",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "\\$ 35"
        },
        "metadata": {
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "to rent the venue and",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "\\$ 10.25"
        },
        "metadata": {
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "per attendee. The event planner has a budget of",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "\\$ 200"
        },
        "metadata": {
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ". What is the greatest number of attendees possible without exceeding the budget?",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "p"
          ],
          "content_type": "stem"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "blank"
      }
    ],
    "explanation": [
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "The correct answer is",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "16"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ". The total cost of the party is found by adding the onetime fee of the venue to the cost per attendee times the number of attendees. Let",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "x"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "be the number of attendees. The expression",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "35 + 10.25 x"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "thus represents the total cost of the party. It's given that the budget is",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "\\$ 200"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", so this situation can be represented by the inequality",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "35 + 10.25 x \\leq 200"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ". The greatest number of attendees can be found by solving this inequality for",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "x"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ". Subtracting",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "35"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "from both sides of this inequality gives",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "10.25 x \\leq 165"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ". Dividing both sides of this inequality by",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "10.25"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "results in approximately",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "x \\leq 16.098"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ". Since the question is stated in terms of attendees, rounding",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "x"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": "down to the nearest whole number,",
        "metadata": {
          "style": []
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": {
          "type": "latex",
          "content": "16"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "string",
        "content": ", gives the greatest number of attendees possible.",
        "metadata": {
          "style": [
            "p"
          ]
        }
      }
